WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:05.675
Deimos is the smaller and outer of the two natural satellites of Mars, the other being Phobos.

00:06.118 --> 00:14.067
Deimos has a mean radius of 6.2 km (3.9 mi) and takes 30.3 hours to orbit Mars.

00:14.559 --> 00:28.689
Deimos is 23,457.50 km (14,575.81 mi) from Mars, much farther than Mars's other moon, Phobos.

00:29.361 --> 00:34.916
It is named after Deimos, the Ancient Greek god and personification of dread and terror.
